Ladybird serializes the selected rendered text. Blink’s
DomSelection::toString updates layout and passes the visible
range to PlainText with unselectable content excluded.
WebKit’s DOMSelection::toString reads the frame selection.
Gecko’s Selection::Stringify passes SkipInvisibleContent
to its document encoder.

Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 all omitted script,
style, and display:none text. Chrome and Firefox inserted two newlines
between two zero-margin paragraphs. WebKit inserted one. Chrome and
WebKit applied text-transform and omitted image alternative text.
Firefox included the alternative text. All three kept a space between
words across a soft wrap.
